// Deal or Force - the navies of 1 January 2024.
//
// A fleet is hulls at a place. Its home port is worked out from that place - the
// nearest coastal province its owner holds, on the same sea - so a mod writes coordinates
// it can read off any map instead of a province id that moves when the map is recompiled.
//
// The great navies are split the way they are actually based. A Russia with one fleet in
// Vladivostok had nothing in the Baltic or the Black Sea; an America with one in Norfolk
// sent the whole of it through Panama to reach the Pacific. The totals are the same as
// they were: the Pacific Fleet and the Atlantic Fleet together are the 243 hulls the one
// Atlantic Fleet used to be. The one exception is the Black Sea Fleet, which opens 2024 as
// it was then - a third of it sunk or crippled by Ukrainian missiles and sea drones, and what
// was left pulled back from Sevastopol to Novorossiysk.
//
// Listing a country here replaces whatever fleets it had, so a mod that gives one
// country a navy leaves every other country's alone.
//
// Generated by Tools/MapDataCompiler and extended by hand; edit it by hand if you like.
